For everything there are drawbacks. Not all wands can be faultlessly
identified by engraving, there are a couple of duplicate messages, and
about 5 or 6 wands that give no message at all. Engraving also uses a
charge. Rings lost down sinks are always properly identified (so long as
you take proper steps like placing someone else on top of the sink to ID
hunger), but when a ring is identified, it doesn't expire from use the way
a wand does. Doesn't do you a lot of good to engrave-ID a wand of death to
use its last charge up in the process and then not get another one until
Orcus (which doesn't even need engraving).


